# Archify — Cursor AI Project Rules & Reference

> **Purpose:** This file is the single source of truth for this project.
> Load it into Cursor AI as a rule file. Every decision — naming, structure, design, logic — must follow what is defined here.
>
> This file works together with two companion rule files: `cursor-learning-rule.mdc` (how Cursor should guide/teach me step by step) and `system-design-rule.mdc` (deeper architectural patterns). This file covers the project itself: what it is, its schema, its stack, and its build order.

---

## 1. Project Overview

A **multilingual website + admin CMS** for an architecture and interior design consultancy. Public visitors browse services, portfolio projects, the blog/journal, and team info, and submit contact/lead inquiries. A single admin manages all content through a dedicated dark-themed admin panel.

**Brand personality:** Premium, moody, cinematic, warm. Dark cork/wood-inspired palette — not corporate gray, not flat SaaS design.

**Languages:** English (default), Turkish, Arabic (RTL). Static UI strings are translated via Laravel's own localization files; dynamic content (services, projects, blog, etc.) is stored per-locale in `_translations` tables and can be auto-translated via **DeepL**.

