## 2. Tech Stack

| Layer | Technology | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| Backend framework | Laravel 12 | PHP 8.2+ |
| Frontend bridge | Inertia.js v2 | SSR optional, add later if needed for SEO |
| Frontend framework | Vue 3 | Composition API + `<script setup>` only |
| Styling | Tailwind CSS v3 | Utility-first, no inline styles, no custom CSS files unless unavoidable |
| Auth scaffolding | Laravel Breeze | Inertia + Vue preset — **admin login only**, no public registration |
| Image/video management | Spatie Laravel MediaLibrary | All images, galleries, and video uploads across every model |
| SEO-friendly URLs | Native slug columns per locale (see schema) | Not a package — slugs are per-language columns on translation tables |
| Machine translation | DeepL PHP client (`deeplcom/deepl-php`) | Used only inside queued Jobs — never called synchronously in a request |
| Queue driver | **Database** | Chosen specifically because Redis isn't reliably available on shared hosting; see Section 8 |
| Frontend UI | @headlessui/vue | Accessible modals, dropdowns, tabs |
| Frontend utilities | @vueuse/core | Composables (localStorage, debounce, etc.) |
| Rich text editor | Tiptap (or TinyMCE) | Blog content and long descriptions |
| Charts | Chart.js (via vue-chartjs) | Admin dashboard traffic/stats |
| Icons | Tabler Icons (@tabler/icons-vue) | All icons throughout the app, matches the thin-line icon style from the design system |
| HTTP client | Axios | Already included via Laravel |

