## 7. Routing & Locale Strategy

- URL structure: `/{locale}/...` with `en` as default (optionally omitted: `/` = English, `/tr/...`, `/ar/...`)
- A `SetLocale` middleware resolves `{locale}` from the URL segment, validates it against active `languages`, and sets `app()->setLocale()`
- Slugs are **per-language** (from the schema) — the same project has a different slug per locale, resolved via a custom route binding that looks up the translation table by `slug` + current locale
- Admin routes are **not** locale-prefixed (`/admin/...`) — the admin UI language (EN/TR/AR for the interface itself) is a separate concern from content locale tabs

