## 11. Build Order (Development Phases)

### Phase 1 — Foundation
1. Install Laravel 11 + Breeze (Inertia + Vue), configure Tailwind with design tokens
2. Create `languages` table + seed en/tr/ar
3. Create all migrations from Section 5, run `php artisan migrate`
4. Create Models + relationships, apply `OrderedScope` where relevant
5. Set up Repository interfaces + Eloquent implementations + `RepositoryServiceProvider`
6. `HandleInertiaRequests` shared data (current locale, active languages, site settings)
7. Build `AppLayout`, `AdminLayout`, `AuthLayout` shells

### Phase 2 — Translation Infrastructure
8. `TranslateContentJob`, `TranslationDispatchService`, `DeepLTranslatorService`
9. `<TranslationTabs>` shared Vue component
10. Test the full job pipeline end-to-end on the actual shared-hosting target before building content features on top of it

### Phase 3 — Public Shell + Static Content
11. Locale-prefixed routing + `SetLocale` middleware
12. Navbar, Footer, Home page (hero slider + about + services + portfolio preview + testimonials)
13. About page, Team page, FAQ

### Phase 4 — Portfolio & Services
14. Services list/detail
15. Project categories, Projects CRUD (with the 6 media collections), Project detail page
16. Concepts tag system

### Phase 5 — Blog & Leads
17. Blog categories, Blog CRUD (rich text, read-time calculation, views tracking)
18. Contact form + Leads inbox (admin)

### Phase 6 — Admin Panel Polish
19. Dashboard (stats, charts)
20. Media Library screen
21. Translations manager (static UI strings)
22. Site Settings (general, SEO, homepage content tabs)

### Phase 7 — SEO & Launch
23. Meta tags across all pages, sitemap generation, structured data
24. Connect Google Analytics + Search Console post-deployment
25. Final queue/cron verification on production hosting

